# AuthOS Licensing

AuthOS uses different licenses for first-party parts of this repository:

| Path | License |
|------|---------|
| `api/` | GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 only |
| `sso-sdk/` | MIT |
| `packages/authos-cli/` | MIT |
| `packages/authos-node/` | MIT |
| `packages/authos-react/` | MIT |
| `packages/authos-vue/` | MIT |

Vendored third-party code keeps its upstream license notices in place. For example,
[`api/vendor/sqlx-mysql/`](./api/vendor/sqlx-mysql) includes the original SQLx
`LICENSE-MIT` and `LICENSE-APACHE` files as required attribution, but that is not a
separate AuthOS product license.

The canonical license texts are available in [`LICENSES/`](./LICENSES):

- [`LICENSES/AGPL-3.0.txt`](./LICENSES/AGPL-3.0.txt)
- [`LICENSES/MIT.txt`](./LICENSES/MIT.txt)

Package-specific license files are also kept with each publishable package so npm consumers receive the applicable license text.
